  "id": "COMPOUND:26220 - PROTEIN:6340",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Npc16157 and the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, primarily through the CD70 antigen. The CD70 antigen is identified as a target of multiple molecular entities, including (2S)-1-O-3,6,9,12,15-Octadecapentaenoyl-2-O-6,9,12,15-Octadecatetraenoyl-3-O-Beta-D-Galactopyranosylsn-Glycerol and Azelate. Both of these molecules are linked to the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, indicating a possible mechanism of action involving the regulation of gene expression through the polycomb repressive complex 2 (PRC2). The scores from the paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, with the highest score attributed to the direct interaction between Npc16157 and CD70 antigen, followed by the interaction between CD70 and Azelate. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Npc16157 and the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, particularly through the CD70 antigen, which is a known target of multiple molecular entities that interact with the PRC2 complex. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential role of CD70 in mediating the effects of Npc16157 on the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the exact mechanism and functional significance.",
